%[text] %[text:anchor:T_B5838CB7] # Eigenvalues and Eigenvectors
%[text] 
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Guitar](text:image:1849)
%[text] Each string of a guitar vibrates at a fundamental frequency. Additional vibrational modes, known as harmonics, are also present. Together, they produce rich, complementary tones. Natural vibrations like these can be identified by performing an eigenanalysis of a computational model of the system.
%[text] In this script, you'll learn the fundamentals of eigenvectors and eigenvalues. 
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
